We are all in my flat now.
Asha, Rohan, and Priya are with me.
We are standing just inside the open doors of the balcony.
We all have cups of hot chai in our hands.
We are safe inside, so we are completely dry.
Outside, the fiercest rain of this season is happening.
Because of the strong wind, the rain is falling horizontally.
I tell my friends that I really like this stormy weather.
Last week it also rained a lot.
But today, a real storm has arrived!
Rohan looks at the dark sky.
He says, "Maya, the Mumbai monsoon has shown its true form."
Asha laughs and takes a sip of chai.
She says, "Yes, and water has filled our entire street."
Priya asks me, "Do you really like this storm?"
I smile and listen to the sound of the heavy rain.
I say, "Yes, when I came here in January, the city was completely dry."
"Now this rain has completely changed Mumbai."
Watching this view with my friends today is the best gift for my birthday.
